<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>Dubrovnik Old Town Walking Tour - Kim and Dave</name><Placemark><name>0. Start: Pile Gate (orientation only)</name><description>Main entrance to the Old Town. Bus and taxi drop-off from the cruise port.</description><Point><coordinates>18.1068385,42.6417295,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>1. Franciscan Monastery &amp; Church</name><description>Just inside Pile Gate on Stradun. Cloister, Romanesque-Gothic courtyard, one of Europe&#x27;s oldest pharmacies.</description><Point><coordinates>18.1075454,42.6418297,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>2. Sponza Palace</name><description>Halfway down the east end of Stradun. Free to enter. Gothic-Renaissance customs house and archive.</description><Point><coordinates>18.110559,42.6412434,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>3a. St. Blaise Church</name><description>Baroque church of Dubrovnik&#x27;s patron saint, on Luža Square.</description><Point><coordinates>18.1102614,42.6406552,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>3b. Clock Tower (Gradski zvonik)</name><description>Bell tower at the east end of Stradun, beside Luža Square.</description><Point><coordinates>18.1106377,42.6409586,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>4a. Rector&#x27;s Palace</name><description>Gothic-Renaissance palace of the Republic&#x27;s rector, facing the harbor side.</description><Point><coordinates>18.1107276,42.640315,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>4b. Dubrovnik Cathedral</name><description>Baroque Cathedral of the Assumption, Bunićeva Poljana.</description><Point><coordinates>18.1104222,42.6399062,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>5a. Gundulić Square</name><description>Morning market square with the Gundulić monument and baroque paving.</description><Point><coordinates>18.1099257,42.6402091,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>5b. Jesuit Stairs &amp; Church of St. Ignatius</name><description>Baroque staircase rising from Gundulić Square to the Jesuit church. Pin is on the square at the top (Poljana Ruđera Boškovića).</description><Point><coordinates>18.109579,42.6393542,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Document></kml>